### The threshold pair: Tiger God + 大二爷伯

```
LEFT: Tiger God (虎爷)
  Function: apotropaic — guards against evil and disease;
            protects the earth-domain of the compound
  Nature:   earth-bound; inhabits ground-level cave

RIGHT: 大二爷伯 (Big and Second Uncles)
  Function: psychopomp — escorts souls across life/death
            boundary; agents of inescapable divine justice
  Nature:   liminal; inhabit the threshold between
            living and dead worlds

COMPLEMENTARITY:
  Tiger God addresses threats FROM OUTSIDE the compound
  (evil spirits, malevolent forces entering from the world)
  大二爷伯 address transitions TO THE OUTSIDE of life
  (souls departing this world for the underworld)

  Together they cover the full spectrum of threshold
  protection: against unwanted entry (Tiger God)
  and for managed exit (大二爷伯).

CONTRASTED WITH DOOR-GOD PAIR (Loyang Tua Pek Kong):
  Menshen: paired martial generals, purely apotropaic
           (preventing malevolent forces from entering)
  Tiger + 大二爷伯: one apotropaic + one psychopomp
                    (preventing harmful entry + managing
                     death-departure)

  A different institutional theology of the threshold —
  one that acknowledges death as part of the temple's
  functional domain, not merely a danger to be excluded.
```

